    body = phrase {
        payload = "Follow this sequence to learn how ordinary programs grow into reusable language vocabularies. Read in order on your first pass; return to the API reference when you need an exact phrase contract.

## Start with a working program

1. [Install the binary](installation.rl) or [set up VS Code](installation-vscode.rl).
2. [First program](first-program.rl) shows execution, output and assertions.
3. [First project](first-project.rl) organizes source files, tasks, consoles and F5 debugging in VS Code.

## Learn the language

1. [Values](values.rl)
2. [Control flow](control-flow.rl)
3. [Functions](functions.rl)
4. [Native types](types.rl)
5. [Records](records.rl)
6. [Phrases](phrase-model.rl)
7. [Metadata](metadata.rl)
8. [Syntax extensions](syntax.rl)
9. [Libraries](libraries.rl)
10. [Memory](memory.rl)
11. [Foreign functions](foreign-functions.rl)
12. [Native output](native-output.rl)

## Continue with a library

The [Libraries](libraries.rl) chapter maps application needs to standard vocabularies. Each library starts with an overview, followed by a short sequence of concept chapters and then an API reference. Detailed tasks, ownership rules and failure handling appear under the headings on each page."
    }
]
